# WCS Sagas and Projections

Axon saga infrastructure is configured through a JPA saga store and cache, but no application class annotated `@Saga` was found in the current source pass. Long-running coordination is visibly implemented through dispatchers, event listeners, aggregate relationships and agent sessions.

Event processor configuration includes subscribing processors and tracking groups:

- `application-processor`
- `async-processor`
- `agent-processor`

Observed processing groups include `job`, `item`, `transaction` and `async`.

Representative projections/query services:

- `WorkProjector`, `WorkQueryService`
- `ItemProjector`, `ItemMovementProcessor`, `ItemQueryService`
- asset/container/location projectors and query services
- `MessageLogService`, `MessageQueryService`
- `WebhookMonitor`, `WebhookViewQueryService`
- `EventMonitor`, common query services

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  event[Domain event] --> processor[Axon processor]
  processor --> projector[Projector / listener]
  projector --> view[(JPA read model)]
  query[Query handler] --> view
  processor --> followup[Follow-up command/integration]
```

Projection updates can be asynchronous; REST list/status APIs should be treated as eventually consistent read models.

Source: `tes-common/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/common/axon/AxonMessageInterceptorConfig.java`; `tes-common/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/common/projector/persistence/`; `tes-engine/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/engine/work/persistence/WorkProjector.java`; `tes-inventory/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/inventory/item/persistence/ItemProjector.java`; `tes-message-broker/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/agent/`.
